  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set mapping the divergence:\n\n**Babel side:** `packages/babel-plugin-syntax-decorators/src/index.ts` (chooses `legacy` vs `2018-09`/stage-3 form based on the `legacy` option) \u2192 `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` (dispatches transform by `version`, including `\"2018-09\"` and `legacyDecorator` compat) \u2192 `packages/babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/index.ts` (shared class-feature lowering, `decoratorVersion` param governs whether legacy `Reflect.metadata`-compatible output or stage-3 semantics is produced) \u2192 `packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` (must run *after* the legacy decorators plugin in the preset order so class properties aren't stripped before decorators can see them \u2014 CHANGELOG confirms this was a historical bug fix, \"Avoid stripping class properties when a decorator is set\").\n\n**SWC side:** `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` wires `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator`/`decoratorMetadata` config flags (both default `false`) into `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs`, which branches `Either::Left(legacy::new(emit_metadata))` vs. a stage-3 path depending on `legacy_decorator`; `emit_metadata` only takes effect inside the legacy branch, implemented in `decorators/legacy/metadata.rs`.\n\n**The divergence:** Nest.js relies on `Reflect.metadata` design-type emission, which only exists in the **legacy (stage-2)** decorator form. Babel's default preset-typescript path historically required explicit `[\"@babel/plugin-proposal-decorators\", {\"legacy\": true}]` ordered before `plugin-transform-typescript`. SWC's default `jsc.transform` has **both** `legacyDecorator` and `decoratorMetadata` off by default \u2014 so a customer who only sets `legacyDecorator: true` without also setting `decoratorMetadata: true` gets stage-2 decorator *invocation* (classes still construct) but no `design:paramtypes`/`design:type` metadata emitted at all, exactly matching the reported symptom: decorators fire, DI metadata table is never populated, `Reflect.getMetadata` returns `undefined`.",
